WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.333
And I

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:01.768
want to go now to the former CIA

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.336
director and former commander of U.S.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.037
Central Command,

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.506
the retired Army General David Petraeus.

00:00:06.973 --> 00:00:07.340
And General,

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.608
thank you so much for your time.

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.043
So, you know, as we're watching that

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.578
and we were talking about

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.612
Ukraine wants three

00:00:12.612 --> 00:00:13.546
to 400 of these tanks,

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:14.447
but they're getting about

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.182
100 of the combined,

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.217
not all M-1 Abrams,

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.418
but also with the leopards,

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:18.785
you know,

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.587
each of which have their own attributes.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.355
31 Abrams, I guess, 80 leopards.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:23.223
And then the U.K.

00:00:23.223 --> 00:00:24.924
also sending their Challenger tanks.

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.292
So when you look at

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:28.161
what's been promised, what does it mean?

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:28.995
How significantly

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.330
does it change the battle?

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:31.631
Well, it's hugely significant,

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.632
and it's significant

00:00:32.632 --> 00:00:34.801
symbolically that this next step

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.202
is being taken.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:38.371
It's very significant substantively

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.205
on the battlefield.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.807
The tank is the centerpiece

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.742
of combined arms operations,

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:43.109
which are

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.944
what will be necessary

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.813
to have successful offensives

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:47.781
this summer,

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.983
maybe late spring by Ukraine,

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.951
to take back to liberate

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:53.186
more of the territory

00:00:53.186 --> 00:00:54.354
that Russia has occupied

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.423
since 24 February.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:57.991
That tank is the piece around

00:00:57.991 --> 00:01:00.026
which everything else will be built.

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.027
There are infantry fighting

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.462
vehicles were already providing

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:03.630
those training them.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.665
In Germany, there will be artillery.

00:01:05.665 --> 00:01:07.067
We've provided a lot of that.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.169
There'll be air defense engineers,

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:13.606
electronic warfare, EOD drones out front.

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:17.310
But all of this exists to get that tank

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:19.579
to the decisive point on the battlefield

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.082
and to keep it essentially invulnerable

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:24.084
from the various threats

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.418
that could be presented.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.853
And so the tank really is a centerpiece.

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.054
And you're saying the M1 Abrams,

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.756
from your experience with it,

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:33.293
is as impenetrable as a vehicle is exist?

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.194
It's extraordinary.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:35.762
Obviously, during the fight to Baghdad,

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:37.630
I was a two star general

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.466
if employed correctly.

00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.101
And you keep the enemy's infantry away

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:42.602
with their anti-tank guided missiles,

00:01:42.602 --> 00:01:46.306
you clear the obstacles and mines

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.340
and so forth.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:49.576
That one ten, 20 millimeter

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:52.912
cannon is enormously powerful

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.580
and effective,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.448
and it will take out anything else

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.683
that is out there.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.650
But the key is

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:58.351
you've got to have

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.953
those as the centerpiece.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.488
Of course, you've got to train on those.

00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:02.789
And so there will be an effort,

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:03.323
I'm sure,

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.057
very quickly,

00:02:04.057 --> 00:02:05.225
if not already ongoing,

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.127
perhaps training them on our tanks

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.628
before these tanks are procured

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:09.963
by General Dynamics

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:10.797
and then the others

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:11.397
that are going to come.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:11.698
The later

00:02:11.698 --> 00:02:13.233
part twos is from Germany, Poland

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.434
and the other European countries

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:14.934
that have them,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.870
as well as the challengers

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:17.303
And again,

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:18.938
this is only a third of what it is

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:19.873
that Ukraine

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.841
would like to have in a perfect case.

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.343
This is quite a powerful.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:24.711
This is this is a lot

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.513
this is multiple battalions,

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.848
probably two brigades, at least,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:29.582
of armored

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:30.416
and mechanized

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:31.317
infantry forces

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.319
with all of the other elements around it.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.889
And that can be a very powerful punch

00:02:36.389 --> 00:02:37.991
and it could enable them

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:40.026
to break through in some key areas

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:41.628
and ideally

00:02:41.628 --> 00:02:42.462
deny Russia

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.363
that opportunity

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:45.999
to support the elements in Crimea.

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:47.133
Directly from Russia.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.034
So you think this does

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.636
put Crimea on the table?

00:02:49.636 --> 00:02:52.405
I think it puts the support for Crimea.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:53.973
I don't think it puts Crimea.

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:54.974
That's a whole different

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:55.875
military problem.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:56.809
It could enable

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.978
the Ukrainian forces to get

00:02:58.978 --> 00:02:59.646
the multiple arms

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:01.481
rocket system with the precision

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.183
missiles in range to take out

00:03:03.183 --> 00:03:04.584
some of the very important air

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:06.719
and naval bases and so forth in Crimea.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.589
But to sever the ability to support

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:11.491
Crimea would be of enormous

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:13.026
value and enormous importance.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:13.526
Absolutely.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.094
So Russia today called the tanks

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.596
enormously, extremely dangerous,

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.697
saying it takes the conflict

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.065
to a new level of confrontation.

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:21.234
That was the defense ministry.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.803
Putin said this today.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:24.537
Let me just play it

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:27.440
some

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:29.542
tactical units.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.912
I have no doubt that one way or another

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:35.982
sovereignty will be returned to Europe.

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:37.083
Europe, judging

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.818
by the look of things, it's

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.854
going to take a little while longer.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:42.188
All right.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.423
So in it for the long haul.

00:03:43.423 --> 00:03:44.824
But what do you hear here

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:45.592
when you hear that

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:46.693
they're getting ready for an offensive?

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.061
You hear those words.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:48.661
Do you think

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:52.565
a real escalation of a nuclear situation

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.601
is on or off the table right now?

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.703
I think it's unlikely, highly unlikely,

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.137
because I think we've communicated

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.172
effectively to him

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.006
that this would put him

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:02.408
in a worse situation after its use

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.010
than before

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.178
And that has to continue

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.813
to be the message.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.249
Look, we have to do everything we can

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.784
as quickly as we can to enable Ukraine

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.988
to show Russia and to show Putin that

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.522
this is not sustainable,

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:18.024
that this war is not sustainable

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:18.858
on the battlefield

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:20.660
where they have already lost eight times

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.694
as soldiers

00:04:21.694 --> 00:04:22.662
in 11 months,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:24.163
that they lost a nearly ten years

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:24.964
in Afghanistan.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:25.465
And also,

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:25.898
by the way,

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:27.400
through our financial, economic

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.368
and personal sanctions

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.636
and export controls,

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:31.237
which we need to tighten further

00:04:31.237 --> 00:04:33.273
to show Putin is unsustainable at home.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.074
So when it comes to unsustainable,

00:04:35.074 --> 00:04:36.242
a lot of people watching will say,

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:36.509
all right,

00:04:36.509 --> 00:04:37.710
hundreds of thousands of Russians

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.345
have been mobilized,

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:41.681
many of them, some large number of them

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.782
killed already

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:44.117
hundreds of

00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:45.685
thousands of young men when the mobile

00:04:45.685 --> 00:04:47.353
first mobilization started, fled Russia.

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.521
Yes, multiple

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.689
people showed up at the right.

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:51.090
More fled than showed up. Okay.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.292
Then we hear about the mass use

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.993
of prisoners as fighters. Right.

00:04:53.993 --> 00:04:54.861
So it all kind of gives

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:55.461
the impression

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.829
that things are falling apart

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:58.831
and Russia is running out of men,

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:00.099
but it is not really down.

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:01.534
He's actually doubling down.

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:02.769
He's just announced in

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.604
his Ministry of defense has confirmed

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:05.538
that they want to increase

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:07.206
the size of their

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:10.143
armed forces by 150 to 200,000 soldiers.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:10.843
Those numbers

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.445
trying to get the military industry

00:05:12.445 --> 00:05:13.313
stood back up.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:13.646
And again,

00:05:13.646 --> 00:05:15.581
we have to convince him

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.216
that this is not going to achieve

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:17.850
the progress,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:18.718
that this is going to be

00:05:18.718 --> 00:05:20.853
a losing proposition, because until then,

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:23.056
it will not be meaningful negotiations.

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:24.957
And just on this, though, his willingness

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:25.792
that he's putting out there

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:26.793
to continue with this,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.093
the fact

00:05:27.093 --> 00:05:28.227
that there are actually

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.162
the numbers of people,

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:30.396
if you're going to throw them out there

00:05:30.396 --> 00:05:32.098
to die, to do it,

00:05:32.098 --> 00:05:33.399
and a lot more people in Russia,

00:05:33.399 --> 00:05:34.801
which is what they're doing, by the way,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:35.868
they're not well trained,

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:36.769
they're not well equipped.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:37.704
They're just pushing them

00:05:37.704 --> 00:05:39.472
into these battles like Seoul, the DA in

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:40.239
bad mood,

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.874
taking massive casualties

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.876
for very incremental gains.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.311
And what they eventually

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.245
take control of

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:47.780
is they have largely destroyed

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.282
in the process of actually seizing.

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:50.283
We're looking at solid art,

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:51.851
but does Ukraine need actual

00:05:51.851 --> 00:05:52.952
boots on the ground assistance

00:05:52.952 --> 00:05:53.853
to win or not?

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.055
We're not going to do that.

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:58.291
That's just not in the cards whatsoever.

00:05:58.725 --> 00:05:59.859
There is not going to be

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.661
that kind of support

00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:02.462
and these

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:03.629
these lines have been drawn

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:04.564
very, very clearly

00:06:04.564 --> 00:06:05.131
by President

00:06:05.131 --> 00:06:06.899
Biden and NATO's secretary general,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.068
other leaders of NATO's countries.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:10.803
We should be doing everything we can

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.205
to enable Ukraine

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:12.505
by the way,

00:06:12.505 --> 00:06:13.139
keep in mind

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:14.507
that Ukraine, a country less than one

00:06:14.507 --> 00:06:16.409
third, the population of Russia, right.

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:18.878
As out generated forces.

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:19.712
In other words, it's done

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:20.613
better recruiting,

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.614
training and equipping

00:06:21.614 --> 00:06:23.216
and employing

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:24.217
additional combat

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.885
capability supported

00:06:25.885 --> 00:06:28.988
by, you know, $27 billion just in arms

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.556
assistance from the United States

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.458
alone, as well as others.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:32.792
All right.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.394
General Petraeus, thank you very much.

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:34.861
Pleasure.

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.662
Wonderful to see you here on set.

